schemas_inspected.description:
Run the Electrical Rules Check (ERC) on the schematic via kicad-cli and return a list of violations filtered by severity.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__konnect__run_erc(args: {
  // Optional path to write this tool's filtered violation list as JSON (not KiCad's own ERC report)
  output?: string;
  // Path to .kicad_sch file
  schematic: string;
  // Minimum severity to report: 'error', 'warning', 'info'
  severity?: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

Save a project-specific rule or override. Same dot-notation as save_user_config but writes to the project's .konnect/project.json.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__konnect__save_project_config(args: {
  // Dot-notation config key
  key_path: string;
  // Project directory (optional, uses configured default)
  project_dir?: string;
  value: unknown;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

Set board-level design rules (clearance, trace width, via size) in the sibling KiCAD project file.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__konnect__set_design_rules(args: {
  // Path to .kicad_pcb file
  board: string;
  // Minimum clearance in mm
  min_clearance?: number;
  // Minimum hole-to-hole clearance in mm
  min_hole_to_hole?: number;
  // Minimum trace width in mm
  min_trace_width?: number;
  // Minimum via drill diameter in mm
  min_via_drill?: number;
  // Minimum via pad diameter in mm
  min_via_size?: number;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```
